# .windows-known-failures — the native Windows suite result, as a committed
# list of test FILES (prd-25 ruling 2: a count masks a swap; a list is
# falsifiable per file). This is an expected-fail list, not a skip list
# (prd-25 amendment, 2026-08-24): every entry is reported on every run of
# .github/workflows/windows-suite.yml, a failure OUTSIDE it turns the job red,
# and an entry that passes is reported as a removal candidate. Removing an
# entry is an ordinary PR; adding one is not — it needs a cause class below
# and the evidence beside it. Zero entries is the destination.
#
# The measured sha is the commit on main the run was built from, with the
# change that landed this file applied on top. It cannot be the lane's own
# commit: a lane commit is squashed and then cherry-picked into the wave PR,
# so its sha never reaches main, and windows-suite-law.test.ts requires the
# sha to resolve to a real commit in every full clone.
#
# measured: 295b02375293dd05e094c5a4a1ff8b0834bea2b8 node 24.19.0 windows-latest 2026-09-03 https://github.com/launchpad-26/rhizomorph/actions/runs/33706746540
#
# classes (prd-25 ruling 3, one per entry, exactly these seven — six at the
# ruling, fs-semantics by the 2026-09-03 amendment):
#   path-separator       `\` vs `/` in a comparison or a string built by hand
#   drive-letter         C:\ absolutes, file: URLs, path.isAbsolute/resolve on win32
#   procfs               /proc read or a probe that assumes it
#   line-endings         CRLF in an input or an output the test compares bytewise
#   process-signalling   spawn/exec/kill semantics, POSIX binaries, /bin/sh, signals
#   temp-dir             os.tmpdir shape, 8.3 names, EBUSY/EPERM on cleanup, case-insensitive FS
#   fs-semantics         open flags (O_NOFOLLOW), symlink following, ENOTDIR on a file-as-directory
#
